From 263d7cdc7cb8afce58d618d105182128161860e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piyush Jena <jepiyush@amazon.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:19:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] net/bootp: widen the unixtime local in
 grub_dhcp6_session_add

grub_datetime2unixtime writes a grub_int64_t through its second
argument, but grub_dhcp6_session_add declared the local as
grub_int32_t, so the call wrote eight bytes into a four byte object.
send_dhcp_packet already uses grub_int64_t for exactly this call.

GCC 13 accepted the mismatched pointer with a warning. GCC 14 promotes
-Wincompatible-pointer-types to an error:

  net/bootp.c:1061:46: error: passing argument 2 of
  'grub_datetime2unixtime' from incompatible pointer type

Truncation at the assignment to se->transaction_id is still intended,
as that field is a 24 bit bitfield.
---
 grub-core/net/bootp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/grub-core/net/bootp.c b/grub-core/net/bootp.c
index 7baf354..c6161fc 100644
--- a/grub-core/net/bootp.c
+++ b/grub-core/net/bootp.c
@@ -1053,7 +1053,7 @@ grub_dhcp6_session_add (struct grub_net_network_level_interface *iface,
   grub_dhcp6_session_t se;
   struct grub_datetime date;
   grub_err_t err;
-  grub_int32_t t = 0;
+  grub_int64_t t = 0;
 
   se = grub_malloc (sizeof (*se));
 
